WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.177
In lecture two, elimination turned a matrix

2
00:00:06.254 --> 00:00:07.549
into a staircase.

3
00:00:07.549 --> 00:00:10.979
Take the small matrix three, one, six, five.

4
00:00:10.979 --> 00:00:14.180
Its columns are three, six and one, five.

5
00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:18.020
One step, row two minus two times row one

6
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.762
sheared the plane straight down

7
00:00:20.762 --> 00:00:22.923
and gave the staircase U

8
00:00:22.923 --> 00:00:26.330
with columns three, zero and one, three.

9
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.582
Which matrix undoes that step?

10
00:00:29.582 --> 00:00:32.000
Pause and write it down.

11
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.600
To undo a subtraction, add it back

12
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.361
row two plus two times row one.

13
00:00:41.361 --> 00:00:44.122
The inverse is the same matrix

14
00:00:44.122 --> 00:00:47.660
with the sign of the multiplier changed.

15
00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:49.426
Watch the plane.

16
00:00:49.426 --> 00:00:51.462
The shear runs upward

17
00:00:51.462 --> 00:00:54.383
and the columns return to three

18
00:00:54.383 --> 00:00:56.065
six and one, five.

19
00:00:56.065 --> 00:00:57.570
That is A again.

20
00:00:58.150 --> 00:01:01.252
Now the paint matrix from lecture two

21
00:01:01.252 --> 00:01:04.926
with three steps and three multipliers: two

22
00:01:04.926 --> 00:01:06.150
one and three.

23
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.264
Elimination was E three two

24
00:01:09.264 --> 00:01:13.706
times E three one, times E two one, times A

25
00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:14.891
equal to U.

26
00:01:14.891 --> 00:01:18.938
To get A back, multiply by the inverses

27
00:01:18.938 --> 00:01:21.900
and undo the last step first.

28
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:24.910
Multiply those three inverses

29
00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:27.659
and you get a matrix called L.

30
00:01:27.659 --> 00:01:31.472
Below its diagonal sit two, one and three

31
00:01:31.472 --> 00:01:33.689
exactly the multipliers

32
00:01:33.689 --> 00:01:36.970
each in the place where it was used.

33
00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:40.342
Compare the matrix E from lecture two

34
00:01:40.342 --> 00:01:43.060
the product of the steps themselves.

35
00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:45.190
It has a five in its corner.

36
00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.671
No multiplier was five.

37
00:01:47.671 --> 00:01:50.449
In E the steps mix, but in L

38
00:01:50.449 --> 00:01:53.414
the reverse order, they do not.

39
00:01:53.414 --> 00:01:56.100
So L costs nothing to build

40
00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:59.620
write down each multiplier as you go.

41
00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.267
So A equals L times U.

42
00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:04.428
L is lower triangular

43
00:02:04.522 --> 00:02:07.247
with ones on the diagonal and

44
00:02:07.341 --> 00:02:09.409
the multipliers below.

45
00:02:09.409 --> 00:02:12.979
U is upper triangular: the staircase

46
00:02:12.979 --> 00:02:16.080
with the pivots on its diagonal.

47
00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:20.588
Back in the plane, with the small matrix.

48
00:02:20.588 --> 00:02:24.949
A times x is L times U x, so U goes first.

49
00:02:24.949 --> 00:02:28.397
It stretches and leans the plane

50
00:02:28.397 --> 00:02:32.960
the unit arrows land on three, zero and one

51
00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:33.670
three.

52
00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:37.380
Then L shears it upward, onto three

53
00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.833
six and one, five: the columns of A.

54
00:02:40.833 --> 00:02:44.940
Multiply L by U, and you always get A back.

55
00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:46.706
A common slip

56
00:02:46.791 --> 00:02:49.334
putting the minus signs of the

57
00:02:49.418 --> 00:02:51.791
elimination matrices into L.

58
00:02:51.791 --> 00:02:55.520
Here is that wrong L, for the paint matrix.

59
00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.590
Multiply it by U.

60
00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:02.042
Row two comes out as minus four, minus one

61
00:03:02.042 --> 00:03:04.976
zero, not four, three, four.

62
00:03:04.976 --> 00:03:07.910
The wrong L fails the check.

63
00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:11.202
The rule: E gets minus the multiplier

64
00:03:11.202 --> 00:03:13.371
L gets plus the multiplier.

65
00:03:13.371 --> 00:03:16.700
Multiplying back catches the slip at once.

66
00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.602
One more form.

67
00:03:18.602 --> 00:03:20.680
U has the pivots two

68
00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:23.419
one and one on its diagonal.

69
00:03:23.419 --> 00:03:26.724
Divide each row of U by its pivot

70
00:03:26.724 --> 00:03:30.880
and keep the pivots in a diagonal matrix D.

71
00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:34.009
Now A is L times D times U

72
00:03:34.112 --> 00:03:36.891
and both triangular factors

73
00:03:36.994 --> 00:03:39.670
have ones on the diagonal.

74
00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:42.992
What is L U good for?

75
00:03:42.992 --> 00:03:44.167
Solving.

76
00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:49.127
A x equals b is L times U x equals b.

77
00:03:49.127 --> 00:03:52.130
Call U x the vector c.

78
00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:56.472
First solve L c equals b, from the top down.

79
00:03:56.472 --> 00:03:59.648
For the paint order five, fifteen

80
00:03:59.648 --> 00:04:02.098
twenty two, c one is five.

81
00:04:02.098 --> 00:04:05.092
Two c one plus c two is fifteen

82
00:04:05.092 --> 00:04:06.726
so c two is five.

83
00:04:06.816 --> 00:04:09.629
And c one plus three c two plus

84
00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:13.440
c three is twenty two, so c three is two.

85
00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:17.041
That is the right side elimination

86
00:04:17.137 --> 00:04:19.049
gave in lecture two

87
00:04:19.049 --> 00:04:22.778
the forward solve is elimination on b

88
00:04:22.778 --> 00:04:23.926
done later.

89
00:04:24.022 --> 00:04:26.986
Back substitution on U x equals

90
00:04:27.081 --> 00:04:29.950
c then gives one, one and two.

91
00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:33.909
A second customer orders four, eleven

92
00:04:33.909 --> 00:04:34.798
fourteen.

93
00:04:34.798 --> 00:04:38.266
Which parts of the work can you reuse

94
00:04:38.266 --> 00:04:40.489
and which must you redo?

95
00:04:40.489 --> 00:04:42.090
Pause and decide.

96
00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:47.979
Keep L and U as they are

97
00:04:47.979 --> 00:04:51.767
and redo only the two triangular solves.

98
00:04:51.767 --> 00:04:55.369
The answer is one litre of each paint.

99
00:04:55.369 --> 00:04:58.510
The expensive part was done once.

100
00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:02.095
So, two records of elimination.

101
00:05:02.095 --> 00:05:05.101
E is the product of the steps

102
00:05:05.101 --> 00:05:07.136
and its numbers mix.

103
00:05:07.136 --> 00:05:08.881
L is its inverse

104
00:05:08.881 --> 00:05:13.050
and it holds the multipliers as they came.

105
00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:17.630
A equals L U: in the plane, U acts first

106
00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:18.867
and then L.

107
00:05:18.867 --> 00:05:23.200
Factor once, then solve forward and back.

108
00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:27.878
Now you try: solve A x equals three, eight

109
00:05:27.878 --> 00:05:30.696
ten with the paint L and U.

110
00:05:30.696 --> 00:05:33.816
In part two we count the work

111
00:05:33.816 --> 00:05:36.030
and meet zero pivots.
